 ## Overview
-Silhouette Edges is a volumetric gradient-based edge detection method that emphasizes features within a density volume by rendering samples where the gradient is perpendicular to the view direction as opaque black lines [S1, unofficial]. It limits edge visibility to a specific density range to prevent the "thick line" artifact common in kernel density estimates [S1, unofficial].
+Silhouette Edges is a volumetric gradient-based edge detection method that emphasizes features within a density volume by rendering samples where the gradient is perpendicular to the view direction as opaque black lines [S1, unofficial]. It limits edge visibility to a specific density range to prevent the "thick line" artifact common in kernel density estimates [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Volumetric Gradient-Based Edge Detection](22848-volumetric-gradient-based-edge-detection.md) and differs from [LOG-based Silhouette Detection](6322-log-based-silhouette-detection.md) and [Contour Rendering](8471-contour-rendering.md) by operating directly in volume space using gradient-view alignment rather than image-space or Laplacian-based detection [S1, unofficial].
 
